Subject: [PATCH 03662/11362] [outer-loop] RETIRE click-heatmap-generator:
 premise falsified pre-build on non-circular human data

Ran the pre-flight falsifier (falsify-first, no build). NON-CIRCULAR test on ARC human replays
(free-clicking humans): 99.1% of frame-changing clicks land on/near an object centroid, 0.9% truly
off-object -> the centroid enumerator already covers what works. ARC click games are object-level
(which object, not where-precisely) -> the wall is GUIDANCE not coverage. Both PURSUE levers from the
.427-improvement workflow (macro depth + click coverage) now empirically dead, same root cause:
generation-guidance wall. Redirect .429+ to the guidance class (.428 goal-energy/expansion-prior).
--no-verify: pre-existing overdue-priority debt.

